== final-report.md format ==
# Final Report — {{.Feature.ID}}: {{.Feature.Name}}

## Status
ready-for-review / needs-attention

## Summary
1-3 sentences: what was built and whether it meets the acceptance criteria.

## Acceptance Criteria
| # | Criterion | Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | ... | PASS/FAIL | file:line or test output |

## Round History
For each round, summarize:
- What the coder did
- What the reviewer found (and whether it was fixed in a later round)
- What the tester found
- What the deep reviewer found

### Round 1
...
### Round N
...

## All Issues Raised
Consolidate every issue from every reviewer/tester/deep-reviewer across all rounds.
For each issue:
- **Source**: which role, which round
- **Severity**: CRITICAL / WARNING / INFO
- **Status**: FIXED (in round N) / OPEN / WONT-FIX (with justification)
- **Summary**: one-line description
- **File**: file:line

### Issues Summary
| # | Source | Round | Severity | Status | Summary |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | reviewer | 1 | WARNING | FIXED (round 2) | ... |
| 2 | deep-reviewer | 2 | CRITICAL | FIXED (round 3) | ... |

## Remaining Concerns
List any OPEN issues or risks the human reviewer should pay attention to.
If none, write "None — all issues resolved."

## commit-plan.md format ==
# Commit Plan — {{.Feature.ID}}

## Files Changed
List all files modified, created, or deleted.

## Suggested Commits
Break changes into logical commits (if not already committed):
1. commit message — files
2. commit message — files

## Pre-Merge Checklist
- [ ] All acceptance criteria pass
- [ ] No CRITICAL or WARNING issues remain open
- [ ] Tests pass: (list verify commands)
- [ ] Docs updated (if applicable)

